# pax REQ-TO-TEST Matrix

| Requirement | Description | Test |
|---|---|---|
| R1 | PAX output uses extended headers when values exceed ustar limits. | `tests/pax/test_pax.sh` case `pax_extended_header_roundtrip` |
| R2 | Read legacy ustar and cpio newc and convert to pax. | `tests/pax/test_pax.sh` cases `interop_tar_to_pax` and `interop_cpio_to_pax` |
| R3 | Substitution rules apply deterministically in declaration order. | `tests/pax/test_pax.sh` case `subst_order` |
| SEC-1 | Extraction rejects unsafe traversal and absolute extraction paths by default. | `tests/pax/test_pax.sh` case `safe_extract` |
| MODE-1 | Supports `-r`, `-w`, and `-r -w` copy behavior. | `tests/pax/test_pax.sh` cases `roundtrip_rw` and `copy_mode` |
